21.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {} 
The only black group that looks close to capture is the C1-C2 two-stone group, with the two liberties B1 and B2. The natural try is B1 to put it in atari. After White B1 Black can defend by playing B2 and linking A2, B3-B4 and C1-C2 into one big connected group. That merged group then has the three outside liberties A1, A3 and A4, so White can only remove one liberty per move and Black can always keep a liberty alive. 

Any other White first point either leaves C1-C2 with two liberties, reduces a group that was already three liberties away, or creates a capture threat that Black can use to gain time. Against perfect defence Black can always keep at least one liberty for the merged group, so White cannot force a capture on the first move and no killing sequence is forced.

