12.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: The board and liberty structure is stable from earlier rounds.

Black sub-groups before White move:
G_A = A2 with L {A1,A3,B2}
G_B = B3–B4 with L {A3,A4,B2}
G_C = C1–C2 with L {B1,B2}
B2 is the common liberty of G_A,G_B,G_C. White wall D1 D2 C3 C4 B5 seals the right/top side of C1–C2.

Current round discussion repeats the two main candidate first moves.

W B1:
W B1 has L {A1,B2} and leaves G_C with unique liberty B2.
The defence 2.B B2 is legal under group liberties. After B2 the stones A2,B2,B3,B4,C1,C2 become one group M with distinct empty neighbours A1,A3,A4. The placed B2 stone is not suicide because M has three liberties; the stone-liberty “four neighbours occupied” reading is wrong. W B1 is now in atari on A1 and A1 is illegal suicide for White. Black can capture W B1 with A1 next move and M lives. No forced capture of Black follows. Colleagues 1,10,11,12,16,17 etc now correctly state B2 is legal.

W B2:
1.W B2 removes B2 from G_A,G_B,G_C. G_C is now in atari on B1 and W B2 itself is in atari on B1, L(W B2)={B1}. Black is forced to answer on B1 or lose C1–C2 immediately. 2.B B1 captures W B2 and connects to C1–C2. After capture:
B1–C1–C2 L {A1,B2}
A2 L {A1,A3,B2}
B3–B4 L {A3,A4,B2}
W A1 is illegal suicide against A2 and B1, W B2 is gone. Any A-file reduction A3/A4 is met by B A4/B A3 or by 3.B B2 which merges the three complexes into A2 B2 B3 B4 B1 C1 C2 with outside liberties A1,A3,A4. White moves second on the A-file after the forced B1 reply and cannot close both A1 and A3/A4 simultaneously. Claims that 3.W A1 is a net capture after 1.W B2 2.B B1 are incorrect because A1 would be zero-liberty self-atari.

W A3 is self-atari on A4 and captured immediately by B A4. W A4 is met by B B2 which merges X,Y,Z into a ≥3-liberty group and puts the White stone in atari. W A1 is captured by B B1.

The minority claims {B1} and {B2} rest on the mistaken suicide assessment of B B2 after W B1 and on the illegal A1 net after W B2. The corrected group-liberty analysis shows Black always has a connecting defence B2 after W B1 and a snap-back B B1 after W B2 which restores a liberty to the merged A2–B3–B4–C1–C2 mass and removes the White atari stone.

No first move puts a Black group into a capture that holds against all Black replies. The consistent forcing claim for B1 or B2 relies on the incorrect suicide assessment. Current belief remains no forcing first move; answer is {}.

Unresolved points are none substantive; the remaining disagreement is entirely the suicide misreading, now largely corrected in the round.

3.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: The earlier mistake that B B2 is suicide after 1.W B1 is now firmly corrected. After 1.W B1 the C1–C2 pair is down to the unique liberty B2 and W B1 has {A1,B2}. B B2 is legal under group-liberty rules: the new stone joins A2, B3, B4, C1, C2 into M = A2 B2 B3 B4 C1 C2 whose distinct empty neighbours are A1, A3, A4. The move does not capture W B1, which still retains A1. After 1.W B1 2.B B2 White B1 is in atari on A1 only and A1 is illegal suicide for White, so B A1 captures W B1 and the merged left side lives with ≥3 liberties. No forced capture of Black follows.

After 1.W B2 the stone itself is in atari on B1 and C1–C2 is down to the unique liberty B1. Black is forced to 2.B B1 which captures W B2 and forms B1–C1–C2. After the capture B2 is empty again, so
* Z = B1–C1–C2 L = {A1,B2}
* X = A2 L = {A1,A3,B2}
* Y = B3–B4 L = {A3,A4,B2}
W A1 is suicide against A2 and B1, W B2 is suicide against A2,B1,B3,C2, and any A-file pressure A3/A4 is met by B A4 capturing the atari White stone or by 3.B B2 merging X,Y,Z into M with outside liberties A1,A3,A4. The claimed net W A1 after 1.W B2 2.B B1 is illegal because Z and X both still retain B2 and the B3–B4 chain retains A3/A4.

A-file first moves are self-atari or immediate capture: W A3 is captured by B A4, W A4 is answered by B B2 merging the left side and putting the White stone in atari, W A1 is captured by B B1. All other first points leave C1–C2 with two liberties.

Hence White can obtain temporary atari on C1–C2 with B1 or B2, but Black always has a legal connecting defence B2 after W B1 and the snap-back capture B1 after W B2 which restores a liberty to the merged A2–B3–B4–C1–C2 mass and removes the White atari stone. No first White point initiates a kill that is forced against all Black replies. The set of forcing killing first moves is empty. The persistent disagreement in the room is between the {} majority and the minority B2 / B1 / A3 claims; the minority claims rely on reading B2 as stone-suicide after W B1 and on an illegal A1 net after W B2  B B1, both of which are refuted by group-liberty accounting.

